WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-22, with W4 (0.0.3)


STATE

  Version 0.0.3, variables and parameter expansion, on branch dev. It
  adds the variable table (src/var.c: shell/export/readonly flags,
  environ import, lazy envp rebuild), structured word parts (tc_wpart),
  assignment-only and prefix assignments (with POSIX special vs regular
  builtin persistence), POSIX parameter expansion (${x:-w}, ${x:=w},
  ${x:?w}, ${x:+w} with and without ':', ${#x}, plain-string %/%%/#/#),
  unquoted here-document parameter expansion, special and positional
  parameters ($? $$ $! $# $@ $* $- $0 $1..${10}+), tilde expansion,
  PS1/PS2 variables, and logical/physical cd (-L/-P, PWD, OLDPWD,
  CDPATH). readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize
  pass (255 unit checks, 65 script/startup checks against bash --posix).

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0; unquoted expansions containing IFS characters pass
  through as a single word until field splitting lands in 0.1.0.


